    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16338" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Euhius</span></b>  (cf. Lach. ad <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
		743</span></i>; also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Euius</span></b> ; less
		correctly, as in some edd., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Evius</span></b> ),
			ii, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a surname of Bacchus</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
			742</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 25, 60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				18, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 11, 17</span></i>; Col. poët. 10,
				424.—<i>Acc.</i> Euhion, <i><span class="en">Pers. 1,
			102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 1, 563</span></i>; voc.
			Euhie, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 2, 72</span></i>; Col. poët.
			10, 224.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Euhius</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Evius</span></b> ), a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Bacchus</i>, <i>Bacchic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terga, i. e. tympana,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Ach. 2, 15</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Euhĭas</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>a
				Bacchante</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 25, 9</span></i>.</div>
